HOL4 conditional/contextual simplifier
======================================

simpLib is the simplifier, and congLib simplifies with respect to
preorders other than equality.  Both are built on Traverse, Cond_rewr,
Opening and Travrules; pureSimps, boolSimps and combinSimps provide the
basic fragments.

simpExtLib is an opt-in extension of the simplifier, adding solvers,
loopers, split rules, configurable side-condition handling and child-first
traversal; congExtLib extends congLib in the same way.  Loading simpLib or
congLib does not load them.  Their reference documentation is in
help/Docfiles/simpExtLib.*.smd.

src/notes.md describes the main types and how the modules fit together;
src/MANIFEST summarises each file.
